    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are two non-singular matrices of order <math><mn>3</mn></math> such that <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi></math>, then the value of <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to (where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is the null matrix of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>)",
